.TH lman 1 (date) "Linux man-pages (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
lman
\-
local man
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY lman
.RI [ man-options ]
.I page
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B lman
command renders a manual page from a local file.
It is equivalent to
.IR man\~\-l .
All the arguments are interpreted by
.BR man (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1)
